import{_ as i,o,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 528 | Myriad-Races Self-Chosen-Destiny Mechanism | Alaya Supervision of Self-Chosen Destiny","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 528 | Myriad-Races Self-Chosen-Destiny Mechanism | Alaya Supervision of Self-Chosen Destiny","no":528,"module":3,"tags":["Myriad-Races Self-Chosen-Destiny","Alaya Network","Multi-Layer Supervision","Freedom Boundaries","Anti-Coercion"],"related":["21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principles","40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0528_模块3-自选命运阿赖耶监管.md","filePath":"en/0528_模块3-自选命运阿赖耶监管.md"}'),s={name:"en/0528_模块3-自选命运阿赖耶监管.md"};function a(r,e,l,c,d,u){return o(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-528-myriad-races-self-chosen-destiny-mechanism-alaya-supervision-of-self-chosen-destiny" tabindex="-1">Entry 528 | Myriad-Races Self-Chosen-Destiny Mechanism | Alaya Supervision of Self-Chosen Destiny <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-528-myriad-races-self-chosen-destiny-mechanism-alaya-supervision-of-self-chosen-destiny" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 528 | Myriad-Races Self-Chosen-Destiny Mechanism | Alaya Supervision of Self-Chosen Destiny&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain | Benchmark base: Documents 21, 40, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-freedom-needs-guardrails-but-guardrails-cannot-become-cages" tabindex="-1">Introduction: freedom needs guardrails, but guardrails cannot become cages <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-freedom-needs-guardrails-but-guardrails-cannot-become-cages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: freedom needs guardrails, but guardrails cannot become cages&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Once the self-chosen-destiny mechanism opens, people will worry: will someone use the name of &quot;freedom&quot; to predate others? Will someone use the name of &quot;choice&quot; to harm himself? Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer is: <strong>freedom must be supervised, but supervision itself must also be supervised.</strong> The Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s role in the self-chosen-destiny domain is not to choose for beings, but to hold the line of &quot;your freedom ends where another&#39;s freedom begins.&quot; Six top-level axioms are supervision&#39;s highest principles: anti-predation axiom is supervision&#39;s core goal; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires supervision equal for all races; collective ascension axiom requires supervision serve co-building not suppression; causal self-discipline axiom requires supervision process auditable; law-first axiom requires supervision rules stable and unchanging. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-three-supervision-goals" tabindex="-1">I. Three Supervision Goals <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-supervision-goals" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Supervision Goals&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Anti-coercion</strong>: monitor whether any faction forces individuals to choose a path;</li><li><strong>Anti-harm</strong>: monitor whether individuals make irreversible self-destructive choices;</li><li><strong>Anti-shifting</strong>: monitor whether individuals&#39; choices come at the cost of predating others.</li></ol><h2 id="ii-four-supervision-layers" tabindex="-1">II. Four Supervision Layers <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-four-supervision-layers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Four Supervision Layers&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Subject</th><th>Duty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Layer 1</td><td>Alaya automatic monitoring</td><td>Sweep coercion signals, harm signals, shifting signals</td></tr><tr><td>Layer 2</td><td>Myriad-Rank representative group</td><td>Accept individual appeals, mediate choice disputes</td></tr><tr><td>Layer 3</td><td>Anchor Supervisory Committee</td><td>Review large-scale racial-level choice disputes</td></tr><tr><td>Layer 4</td><td>Symbiotic Court</td><td>Adjudicate &quot;self-chosen destiny infringed&quot; cases</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="iii-what-supervision-does-not-do" tabindex="-1">III. What Supervision Does Not Do <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-what-supervision-does-not-do" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. What Supervision Does Not Do&quot;">​</a></h2><p>It must be made clear, the Alaya Network in the self-chosen-destiny domain <strong>does not</strong> do the following:</p><ul><li>Does not decide for the individual &quot;which road is better&quot;;</li><li>Does not record individual thought tendencies for judgment;</li><li>Does not block individuals choosing &quot;seemingly unprofitable&quot; roads;</li><li>Does not look down on a race because it chose &quot;slow.&quot;</li></ul><p>Supervision&#39;s purpose is to protect freedom, not restrict freedom.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-paternalism-narrative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With &quot;Paternalism&quot; Narrative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-paternalism-narrative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With &quot;Paternalism&quot; Narrative&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory-school systems often in the name of &quot;for your own good&quot; decide for the weak — sect masters choose cultivation methods for disciples, dynasties choose destiny for the people, protagonists choose direction for the world. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s self-chosen-destiny supervision is the reverse: <strong>&quot;for your own good&quot; cannot be the reason to deprive the right to choose.</strong> If a being&#39;s choice will truly harm himself, what the system provides is information, advice, exit ramps, not forced blocking.</p><h2 id="v-fast-track-for-supervision-grievances" tabindex="-1">V. Fast-Track for Supervision Grievances <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-fast-track-for-supervision-grievances" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Fast-Track for Supervision Grievances&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Supervision disputes in the self-chosen-destiny domain are often time-sensitive — a being if being forced onto a path, delaying a week may be irreversible trauma. For this, the Symbiotic Court opened a fast track for &quot;self-chosen destiny infringed&quot; cases: from submitting grievance to initial adjudication no more than three reality days; in emergencies a temporary protection order may be issued within twenty-four hours, pausing the complained-of coercive behavior. The fast track&#39;s existence keeps supervision from becoming de facto indulgence in lengthy procedures.</p><h3 id="anti-coercion-institutional-backstop" tabindex="-1">Anti-Coercion Institutional Backstop <a class="header-anchor" href="#anti-coercion-institutional-backstop" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Anti-Coercion Institutional Backstop&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The supervision mechanism has a hard rule of &quot;anti-coercion&quot;: any agency, any mentor, any same-race elder may not in the name of &quot;for your own good&quot; choose a path for the individual. The system by design strictly separates &quot;suggestion&quot; from &quot;decision&quot; — suggestions can be unlimited; only the individual himself may press the confirm button. This rule is especially important in cross-race collaboration: history has repeatedly seen events of &quot;strong ones out of goodwill deciding destiny for the weak&quot;; Heng Yuan Zhou by institutions blocks this &quot;well-meaning coercion&quot; as well.</p><h3 id="tension-balance-between-supervision-and-self-choice" tabindex="-1">Tension Balance Between Supervision and Self-Choice <a class="header-anchor" href="#tension-balance-between-supervision-and-self-choice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tension Balance Between Supervision and Self-Choice&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Between self-chosen destiny and supervision exists natural tension: too loose, someone will be predated; too strict, it becomes deciding for people. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s balancing way is: <strong>provide full information before choice occurs; after choice only intercept boundary-crossing behavior, do not intervene in the choice itself.</strong> This is like the traffic light at an intersection — the light tells you which road is safe, but which road you take is still your own decision. Supervisors do not drive; they only do traffic lights.</p><p>Supervision&#39;s highest realm is making the supervised feel no supervision. When rules are internalized into common sense; when coercion only appears at the most extreme boundary-crossing moment, self-chosen destiny and external constraint no longer oppose, but jointly protect everyone&#39;s true freedom.</p><p>Supervision&#39;s ultimate confidence is that one day it can gradually fade — when self-chosen destiny becomes every being&#39;s second nature, supervision only appears at boundary-crossing moments. This is the day institutions hope to retire.</p><p>Supervisors are also mortals, will also err; putting supervisors themselves also under supervision, the whole system will not one day suddenly go bad. This is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39;s last line of defense in governance&#39;s deepest place.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: promptly stop coercion and shifting, avoid individuals and races&#39; energy being predated</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: this entry&#39;s entire core is preventing predation in the name of &quot;choice&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is paternalism; Heng Yuan Zhou is republicanism</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: supervision equal for all races, all individuals</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: three goals, four-layer structure, do-not-do list all public</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Self-chosen destiny is not anarchy, but freedom with guardrails. The Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s existence is not to keep people from choosing, but to let people truly choose — choose without being forced, without being deceived, without being predated.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./21-共生网络运作原理.html">21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principles</a> · <a href="./40-共生宪法总纲.html">40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a> · <a href="./49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">49-Governance Framework and Power Checks</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const m=i(s,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
